Overlay patch 0022: byte-budget texture cache (SYNC WAVE 1; reference 0020).
Fast3D's texture cache is COUNT-based and the Metal backend's DeleteTexture
was EMPTY — evicted ids park on a free list and the MTLTexture is only
released if that id is later reused with different dims. Big texture packs
pin gigabytes and jetsam at menu upload bursts after long sessions. Three
parts (ships even though Starship has no pack ecosystem yet — SYNC WAVE 1
mandate):
1. gfx_rendering_api.h: virtual GetTextureBytes() (default 0 disables the
   budget on other backends).
2. Metal: DeleteTexture actually releases + exact byte ledger (created by
   overlay 0021's UploadTexture accounting); GetTextureBytes reports.
3. interpreter ImportTexture tail (__IOS__): after each upload, evict LRU
   entries until resident bytes <= gSohIos.TexCacheBudgetMB (default 1536),
   keeping >=128 entries. Draws are flushed before imports and command
   buffers retain in-flight textures, so releasing at evict time is
   GPU-safe — the same invariants the count eviction already relies on.

--- a/libultraship/src/graphic/Fast3D/backends/gfx_rendering_api.h
